MBX-RJ-08 an attach rejected twice while /user supervises: the root guardian stops /user and the system terminates -> errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!, LocalActorRefProvider|org.apache.pekko.actor.LocalActorRefProvider|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|guardian failed, shutting down system, pekko://mbx/user|org.apache.pekko.actor.OneForOneStrategy|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|<rejection>] stopped=[c, a] terminated=pekko://mbx/ existenceConfirmed=true refReturned=true rejectionsLeft=0
MBX-DQ-01 the unbounded deque based queue takes an envelope enqueued first at its head, counts it and cleans up from the head -> class=org.apache.pekko.dispatch.UnboundedDequeBasedMailbox$MessageQueue unbounded=true multipleConsumer=true bounded=false | mixed n=4 has=true [d, c, a, b] then null n=0 has=false | onlyFirst [y, x] | cleanUp source n=0 has=false target [c, a, b]
MBX-SCQ-01 the single consumer only unbounded queue is first in first out, counts and cleans up in order, and declares the semantics of Pekko's NodeMessageQueue -> class=org.apache.pekko.dispatch.NodeMessageQueue unbounded=true multipleConsumer=false bounded=false | new n=0 has=false null | n=2 has=true first=a rest=[b, c] n=0 has=false | cleanUp source n=0 has=false target [x, y]
MBX-TT-01 context.actorOf with a mailbox type that throws fails at the call with a ConfigurationException: no child is registered and the name is free -> caught=org.apache.pekko.ConfigurationException: configuration problem while creating [pekko://mbx/user/parent/kid] with dispatcher [pekko.actor.default-dispatcher] and mailbox [failing-mailbox] cause=java.lang.IllegalStateException: mailbox boom log=[children=0, r:m] started=1 errors=[]
MBX-TT-02 system.actorOf with a mailbox type that throws returns: the user guardian stops the actor, keeps serving and the system terminates -> terminated=true log=[r:m] started=1 errors=[pekko://mbx/user/a|org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorInitializationException|mailbox boom] systemTerminated=true
MBX-TQ-01 an enqueue that throws does not reach the caller of tell: an Error is published and the actor goes on -> tell=returned log=[r:a, r:c] dead=[] errors=[pekko://mbx/user/a|java.lang.IllegalStateException|swallowing exception during message send] terminated=false
MBX-TQ-02 a dequeue that throws ends the turn with an uncaught-error report: the thread survives and the queued messages are processed -> log=[r:block, r:a, r:c, r:d] dead=[] errors=[org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorSystemImpl(mbx)|java.lang.IllegalStateException|Uncaught error from thread [mbx-pekko.actor.default-dispatcher-N]] terminated=false
MBX-TQ-03 a hasMessages that throws at the end of a turn is reported as uncaught: the next send schedules the actor again -> log=[r:bad, r:c] errors=[org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorSystemImpl(mbx)|java.lang.IllegalStateException|Uncaught error from thread [mbx-pekko.actor.default-dispatcher-N]] terminated=false
